  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Through FY2026 to date federal contract obligations in Illinois total $8.1B, spread across 356,404 awards with an average award size of $22.8K. Obligations fell 34.3% year over year, and current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress. Recent fiscal-year listings show higher totals in prior years, with FY21 at $12B, FY22 at $13.6B, FY23 at $13B, FY24 at $13.4B, and FY25 at $12.4B. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer in the state with $4B in obligations, followed by the Department of Energy and the Department of Veterans Affairs, each at $1.6B. Top vendors in FY2026 to date include UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC at $913M, W S DARLEY & CO at $790M, and MEDLINE INDUSTRIES, LP at $772M. Medical and research-related industries dominate the sector list, led by Medical, Dental, and Hospital Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers at $981M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $913M. This snapshot shows where federal dollars and contract activity are concentrated in Illinois so far this fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Illinois?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $4B in obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of Energy and the Department of Veterans Affairs each account for $1.6B. Other significant buyers include the General Services Administration at $376M and the Department of Agriculture at $167M. Smaller but notable buyers listed are the Department of Health and Human Services at $158M and the Department of Homeland Security at $68.8M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest contractors and which industries win work?",
        "body": "UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC is the largest contractor at $913M, followed by W S DARLEY & CO at $790M and MEDLINE INDUSTRIES, LP at $772M. Industry winners are centered on medical supplies and research, led by Medical, Dental, and Hospital Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers at $981M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $913M. Other industry categories with substantial obligations include Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers at $500M and All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing at $447M."
      }
